From d15e2f7e5d377596478fac6466935be0852fee99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:00:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/45] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: selected text takes the colours
 of its ::selection

Selections were painted in a fixed highlight, with the text in its own
colours. Node::selection_styles gives an element's ::selection style
(Stylo computes it eagerly). A text's highlight is its inline root's
::selection background, or the default one when it sets none, as the
user agent's rule for it would; and where a ::selection style exists,
the selected text is stroked again over the highlight, clipped to it, in
each run's ::selection colour (decorations in currentColor follow). Text
inputs do the same with their editor's selection.
